  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NULL - Indonesia (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia, Tuberculosis, Central Board of &#x2018;Aisyiyah (AISYIYA)This program has the following goals: To reduce HIV and TB related morbidity and mortality in thirty four provinces of Indonesia and to strengthen health and community systems in order to improve performance. The objectives of this program are: Ensure treatment success of 90% for drug-sensitive TB treatment in hospitals, the private and public sector by 2019 ..  Ensure universal access to diagnosis and treatment for drug-resistant TB by 2018 and beyond (80% of estemated MDR cases are diagnosed &amp; treated).  Increase the case notification rate for all forms of TB from 130/100,000 in 2013 to 236/100,000 by 2019..  To increase effective interventions to achieve universal access to prevention of TB infection and care, support, and treatment of TB for key affected populations at higher risk, people living with HIV and general population</narrative>
  </description>
